  "assessment": {
    "P14": "Neutral transient occurrence/intra-item/control adapter, synchronous lazy-readiness bridge, cancellable trusted transaction and actual compiled Classic/Studio consumer regressions. Native acceptance remains open; other consumers need their own semantic mapping.",
    "C00": "Flat Favorites, platform details and growing platform overview have default-closed candidates. Full selection/order/actions remain controlled by the existing collection. Newly measured row heights refresh same-identity drag geometry, source grabbed position and frozen release rebasing; incompatible structural changes cancel.",
    "overview": "Original CollectionGrid 320/480/240px widths, gaps and container-based mobile rules retained; real cards, complete group selection, bounded offscreen retention and semantic return offset before focus. Platform grouping is one pass; track-to-platform reorder comparisons use a controlled-result index instead of repeated full scans.",
    "structure": "Injected CSS/box Node fixtures cover 0/1/80/1,000/10,000 platform and track occurrences. Mounted platform slots stay within 15 initially and 24 for distant windows under the recorded fixture; retained interactions remain bounded. These are synthetic structure assertions, not browser-computed layout or total product component/FPS counts.",
    "motionLimit": "Natural measurement is accepted while dragging and through the frozen controlled landing handoff. Reflow after landing motion starts retains the established cancellation behavior. A changed measurement generation still rebuilds the derived spatial index in O(N); pointer and ordinary scroll do not trigger that rebuild. No frame-time bound is claimed."
  },
